    id: 'ai900-771',
    question: "Which statement is an example of a Microsoft responsible AI principle?Select the correct option.",
    options: ["AI systems must be transparent and inclusive.","AI systems must protect the interests of the company.","AI systems must keep personal details public.","AI systems must use only publicly available data."],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    type: 'single',
    explanation: "Option AI systems must be transparent and inclusive is \ncorrect – Transparency and inclusivity are important aspects of AI \nsystems. Transparency refers to the ability of an AI system to explain \nhow it arrived at a decision or recommendation. This is important \nbecause it helps users understand how the system works and builds trust \nin the technology. Inclusivity refers to the ability of an AI system to \nwork for everyone, regardless of their background or identity. This is \nimportant because AI systems can sometimes perpetuate biases and \ndiscrimination if they are not designed with inclusivity in mind.Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cloud-adoption-framework/innovate/best-practices/trusted-ai#transparencyOption AI\n systems must use only publicly available data is not correct – AI \nsystems can use both publicly available and private data, depending on \nthe use case and the datas availability. Publicly available data is \noften used to train AI models, but it is not a requirement. In fact, \nsome AI models require private data to be effective. However, when using\n private data, it is important to ensure that the data is collected and \nused ethically and legally.Option AI systems must keep personal\n details public is not correct – AI systems must not keep personal \ndetails public. In fact, AI systems must be designed to protect the \nprivacy of individuals and their personal data. As AI technology \nevolves, it has the potential to use personal information in ways that \ncan intrude on privacy interests. Therefore, it is important to surround\n AI with policies and procedures that make the most of its potential by \nreducing its risks.Option AI systems must protect the interests\n of the company is not correct – AI systems must not prioritize the\n interests of the company over other considerations. In fact, AI systems\n must be designed to be transparent, inclusive, and ethical.",
    documentationUrl: "",
