    question: "Which of the provided options is considered the calculated probability of a correct image classification?Select the correct option.",
    options: ["Confidence","Sentiment","Root Mean Square Error","Accuracy"],
    correctAnswer: 'A',
    type: 'single',
    explanation: "Option Confidence is correct – The calculated probability \nof a correct image classification refers to the confidence \nlevel of the classifier in its prediction. In general, a classifier\n will output a probability for each possible class, indicating the \nlikelihood that the input image belongs to each class. The class with \nthe highest probability is chosen as the predicted class.For \nexample, consider a classifier that has been trained to recognize three \nclasses: “cat“, “dog“, and “bird“. If the classifier is given an image \nof a cat, it might output the following probabilities:“cat“: 0.8“dog“: 0.1“bird“: 0.1In\n this case, the classifier is 80% confident that the image belongs to \nthe “cat“ class, and so it would predict the label “cat“ for this image.The\n calculated probability of a correct image classification can be useful \nin a number of ways. For example, it can be used to evaluate the \nperformance of a classifier, or to set a threshold for the minimum \nprobability required to make a prediction. It can also be used to \nindicate the uncertainty of a prediction, which can be helpful in \ncertain applications.Reference: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-\nus/azure/cognitive-services/custom-vision-service/getting-started-build-\na-classifier",
