    question: "Consider the below scenario:Scenario:Ensuring that the numeric variables in training data are on a similar scale.The above scenario is an example of which of the following category?",
    options: ["model training","feature engineering","feature selection","data ingestion"],
    correctAnswer: 'B',
    type: 'single',
    explanation: "Option feature engineering is correct – Feature \nengineering is the process of constructing new features or \ntransformations of the available data to improve the performance of a \nmachine learning model. It can involve a variety of techniques, such as \nscaling or normalizing the data, aggregating raw data into more \nmeaningful features, or creating new features based on domain knowledge.Scaling\n or normalizing the data is important because many machine learning \nalgorithms use some form of distance measure to compare data points. If \nthe variables are on different scales, the distance between points will \nbe dominated by the variables with the larger scale, which can distort \nthe model‘s ability to learn from the data. Ensuring that the numeric \nvariables in the training data are on a similar scale helps to balance \nthe influence of the different variables and improve the model‘s \nperformance.Option data ingestion is not correct – \nEnsuring that the numeric variables in training data are on a similar \nscale is not an example of data ingestion. Data ingestion refers to the \nprocess of importing data into a system for processing or analysis. It \ntypically involves extracting the data from its source, transforming it \ninto a usable format, and loading it into the system.Option feature\n selection is not correct – Ensuring that the numeric variables in \ntraining data are on a similar scale is not an example of feature \nselection. Feature selection is the process of selecting a subset of the\n available features or variables to use as input to a machine learning \nmodel. The goal of feature selection is to select a set of features that\n are relevant to the problem and that will improve the model‘s \nperformance, while minimizing the number of features to reduce the \ncomplexity of the model and avoid overfitting.Option model \ntraining is not correct – Ensuring that the numeric variables in \ntraining data are on a similar scale is not an example of model \ntraining. Model training is the process of fitting a machine learning \nmodel to a set of training data. It involves using an optimization \nalgorithm to adjust the model‘s parameters to minimize the error between\n the model‘s predictions and the true values of the target variable in \nthe training data.",
    documentationUrl: "",
